Adapted standard agent-file identity and truncation behavior from Hermes Agent.
Revision: f3ef9db68332063a3625661f3a9b259f60abdb4e
Sources: agent/prompt_builder.py::load_soul_md, _truncate_content;
agent/system_prompt.py::_identity_parts, _context_files_part.
Anima differences: pure host-agnostic rendering, Unicode scalar 70/30 head/tail
allocation including markers and framing, aggregate caps, transient identity and
separate immutable host guidance. No filesystem discovery or threat scanner here.
Fixtures are invented test strings; no upstream private configuration used.
M23 adapts budget-exhaustion wrap-up behavior from Hermes Agent at public tracked
revision 1fd18277267152893a8a24792b79213e7ca3f899:
agent/chat_completion_helpers.py::handle_max_iterations and
agent/turn_finalizer.py::_resolve_budget_fallback.
Anima differences: existing tool-round budget/default retained; one already-next
model turn with explicit empty tools, hard rejection of returned tool calls,
system guidance rather than a synthetic user message, evaluator acceptance and
budgetWrapup provenance. No summary retry or fallback after a terminal failure.
No upstream Python runtime, personal profile or credentials are imported.

M24 adapts the advisory exact-failure pattern from the same public revision:
agent/tool_guardrails.py::ToolCallGuardrailController.after_call.
Anima differences: three consecutive fresh single-call typed failures with
identical canonical arguments/error, one transient fixed system warning, bounded
digest-only per-run state. Successful/malformed/recovered/parallel rounds reset;
no name-based effect inference, result rewriting, hard stop or added model turn.
Upstream defaults its exact-failure warning threshold to two; Anima uses three.

M25 adapts paired validation-refusal continuation from the same public revision:
agent/turn_tool_validation.py::validate_tool_calls.
Anima differences: one fresh bounded single unconfigured call can receive a
static paired error within the existing tool-round budget; a second refusal,
malformed/batched request or reused ID remains terminal. No name correction,
grant changes, executor/action witness, independent repair request or effect
replay. The refusal state is per invocation; native host authorization remains
authoritative for configured calls.

